<header><h1>The Nekro Virus</h1></header>
<article>
<h2 id="galactic-threat"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Galactic%20Threat">Galactic Threat</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Nekro player makes their prediction during the same timing window as riders, after any &ldquo;when an agenda is revealed&rdquo; abilities, such as the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Veto"><i>Veto</i></a> action card or the <a href="/F_xxcha">Xxcha</a> player&rsquo;s Quash faction ability. They must predict an outcome; abstaining is not an outcome.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <ol><li>The Nekro player may still play rider action cards.<sup>1,2</sup></li></ol>
    <li>If the Nekro player has the <a href="/F_xxcha">Xxcha</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Alliance"><i>Alliance</i></a> promissory note, the Nekro player may vote, without losing their ability to predict outcomes for their <sc>Galactic Threat</sc> ability.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If the speaker breaks a tie without casting any votes, then the speaker&rsquo;s technologies are ineligible to be gained.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <ol><li>If no player casts votes, then no technology can be gained.<sup>2</sup></li></ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="technological-singularity"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Technological%20Singularity">Technological Singularity</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the Nekro player gains a technology during a space combat, this does not prevent them from gaining technology during ground combats in the <b>Invasion</b> step of the same tactical action.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If multiple ground combats happen on separate planets as part of a single <b>Invasion</b> step during one action, the Nekro player may gain a technology during each combat.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>Any method that destroys a unit during combat will trigger <sc>Technological Singularity</sc>, including an anti&ndash;fighter barrage roll, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Direct%20Hit"><i>Direct Hit</i></a> action card, the <a href="/F_creuss">Creuss</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Dimensional%20Splicer"><i>Dimensional Splicer</i></a> faction technology, etc.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <ol>
        <li>This includes any method used by the Nekro player&rsquo;s opponent that destroys their own units, usually as an ability cost.<sup>2</sup></li>
        <li>If a unit is removed, but not destroyed, that unit will not trigger the <sc>Technological Singularity</sc> ability.<sup>2</sup></li>
        <li>Space cannon and bombardment rolls happen outside of combat. Any hits produced cannot be used to trigger the <sc>Technological Singularity</sc> ability.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>
    <li>If the Nekro player chooses to gain a unit upgrade technology, that upgrade will be in effect from that point in the combat onwards.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <ol>
        <li>The combat value of a combat dice is fixed as it is rolled, and all combat dice are rolled before any hits are assigned. Gaining a unit upgrade technology will not cause any already rolled combat dice to produce any additional hits due to an improved combat value. The same applies to unit ability dice.<sup>*</sup></li>
        <li>Destroying an opponent&rsquo;s unit during the <b>Anti&ndash;Fighter Barrage</b> step, and gaining a unit upgrade technology will allow units of that type to use the abilities and attributes of the upgrade for the combat rolls of the same round.<sup>2</sup></li>
        <li>Destroying an opponent&rsquo;s unit at the start of a combat, such as with the ability of the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Assault_Cannon"><i>Assault Cannon</i></a> technology, and gaining a unit upgrade technology with an <a href="/R_anti_fighter_barrage"><sc>Anti&ndash;Fighter Barrage</sc></a> ability will allow units of that type to use that ability during the <b>Anti&ndash;Fighter Barrage</b> step of the first round of combat.<sup>2</sup></li>
        <li>If the Nekro player uses the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Direct%20Hit"><i>Direct Hit</i></a> action card to destroy a unit when it uses its <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability, this will occur before any units are destroyed from being assigned hits. If the Nekro player then gains a technology that gives their units the <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability, they may then use that ability for their units participating in the combat to cancel hits produced by their opponent during that round of combat.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>
    <li>If the Nekro player destroys a unit, and gains a technology with an ability that is used during the same timing window, they may use that ability immediately.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <ol><li>For example, if the Nekro player uses the ability of the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Assault_Cannon"><i>Assault Cannon</i></a> technology at the start of a space combat to destroy a unit belonging to the <a href="/F_creuss">Creuss</a> player, and thus place a Valefar token on that player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Dimensional%20Splicer"><i>Dimensional Splicer</i></a> faction technology, the Nekro player may immediately use the ability of their Valefar <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Dimensional%20Splicer"><i>Dimensional Splicer</i></a> to produce a hit against one of the <a href="/F_creuss">Creuss</a> player&rsquo;s ships.<sup>*</sup></li></ol>
    <li>If the Nekro player gains the Infantry II unit upgrade from their <sc>Technological Singularity</sc> ability during a combat, any of the Nekro player&rsquo;s infantry destroyed at the same time as the unit used to trigger the <sc>Technological Singularity</sc> ability will be returned to their reinforcements.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <ol>
        <li>If the Nekro player uses a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Direct%20Hit"><i>Direct Hit</i></a> action card to destroy an opponent&rsquo;s unit, and gain the Infantry II unit upgrade, then any infantry destroyed in that <b>Assign Hits</b> step will roll to be placed on the Infantry II card. This will most commonly occur if the Nekro player has infantry participating in space combat via the ability of their flagship, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Flagship:~:text=The%20Alastor"><i>The Alastor</i></a>.<sup>*</sup></li>
        <li>Any infantry destroyed by the <a href="/F_argent">Argent</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Argent_Flight#Destroyer:~:text=Strike%20Wing%20Alpha">Strike Wing Alpha</a> II faction unit ability are destroyed during the <b>Roll Dice</b> substep of the <b>Anti&ndash;Fighter Barrage</b> step. The Nekro player will not have the opportunity to gain the Infantry II unit upgrade until the <b>Assign Hits</b> substep immediately following, and so the destroyed infantry will be returned to their reinforcements.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>
    <li>The Nekro player cannot use <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Relics#Prophecy_of_Kings:~:text=The%20Prophet%27s%20Tears"><i>The Prophet&rsquo;s Tears</i></a> relic to draw an action card when they gain a technology using this ability.<sup>2,4</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="propagation"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Propagation">Propagation</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Nekro player may still resolve the secondary ability of the <a href="/R_technology_sc"><i>Technology</i></a> strategy card, which will instead gain them command tokens. They must still spend a command token from their strategy pool and four resources to do so.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <ol><li>The Nekro player may still benefit from owning the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Minister%20of%20Sciences"><i>Minister of Sciences</i></a> agenda card.<sup>*</sup></li></ol>
    <li>If an ability triggers &ldquo;when&rdquo; a player researches a technology, that ability will still be triggered by the Nekro player.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <ol><li>If the Nekro player owns <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Relics#Prophecy_of_Kings:~:text=The%20Prophet%27s%20Tears"><i>The Prophet&rsquo;s Tears</i></a> relic, they may draw an action card whenever they would research a technology.<sup>4</sup></li></ol>
    <li>If an ability triggers &ldquo;after&rdquo; a player researches a technology, that ability will never be triggered by the Nekro player.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <ol><li>If the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Anti-Intellectual%20Revolution"><i>Anti&ndash;Intellectual Revolution</i></a> law is in play, the Nekro player will not destroy a ship when they would research a technology.<sup>2</sup></li></ol>
    <li>The Nekro player may play the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Prophecy_of_Kings:~:text=Reveal%20Prototype"><i>Reveal Prototype</i></a> action card, gaining three command tokens instead of researching, but only if there is a unit upgrade technology the card could research.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <ol><li>For example, if the Nekro player&rsquo;s only units in the combat are dreadnoughts and fighters, and they already own both Dreadnought II and Fighter II, they cannot play <i>Reveal Prototype</i>.<sup>*</sup></li></ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="antivirus"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=Antivirus">Antivirus</a> <sub>(Promissory Note)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The effect of <i>Antivirus</i> does not prevent the Nekro player gaining a technology from a player via their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Galactic%20Threat"><sc>Galactic Threat</sc></a> ability.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>The player holding <i>Antivirus</i> may only play it at the start of a combat they are participating in.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <ol><li>The Nekro player does not need to be participating in that combat.<sup>*</sup></li></ol>
    <li><i>Antivirus</i> has no effect while it is in a player&rsquo;s hand.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li><i>Antivirus</i> is returned when the system is activated, even if the active player will perform no hostile acts toward the Nekro player this turn.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>Activating a system containing only the Nekro player&rsquo;s structures will still cause <i>Antivirus</i> to be returned.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If an effect other than activating a system during a tactical action places a command token in a system with the Nekro player&rsquo;s units (for example, the primary ability of the <a href="/R_diplomacy"><i>Diplomacy</i></a> strategy card), this will not cause <i>Antivirus</i> to be returned.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="valefar-assimilator"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Valefar%20Assimilator">Valefar Assimilator</a> <sub>(Technology)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>When copying another technology, each <i>Valefar Assimilator</i> may later be used to copy a different faction technology.<sup>2,5</sup></li>
    <li>When copying another technology, <i>Valefar Assimilator</i> will retain its exhausted/readied state. It will not copy the target technology&rsquo;s exhausted/readied state.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <ol>
        <li>The Nekro player may use any ability of the copied technology that does not require exhausting as a cost, even if the <i>Valefar Assimilator</i> card is exhausted.<sup>*</sup></li>
        <li>An exhausted <i>Valefar Assimilator</i> will always ready during the Status Phase, even if it is not currently copying a technology with an exhaust ability.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>
    <li>If the Nekro player would copy a faction&ndash;specific unit upgrade, and they are already copying a faction&ndash;specific unit upgrade of the same type, they must use the same Valefar Assimilator token; they lose the previous faction unit upgrade.<sup>1,2,5</sup></li>
    <li>The Nekro player cannot copy faction&ndash;specific units that have not been upgraded.<sup>1,2</sup></li>
    <li>A faction&rsquo;s mech is not a technology. The Nekro player cannot use a <i>Valefar Assimilator</i> to copy a mech.<sup>1,8</sup></li>
    <li>If the Nekro player has a generic unit upgrade, and gains a faction&ndash;specific unit upgrade, then the faction&ndash;specific version will be in effect. If the faction&ndash;specific unit upgrade is later lost, they revert to the generic unit upgrade.<sup>1,2,5</sup></li>
    <ol>
        <li>Owning two unit upgrades for the same type of unit in this manner only counts as one unit upgrade toward the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Develop%20Weaponry"><i>Develop Weaponry</i></a> and <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition_2:~:text=Revolutionize%20Warfare"><i>Revolutionize Warfare</i></a> objectives.<sup>1,2,5</sup></li>
        <li>If the Nekro player gains a faction&ndash;specific infantry unit upgrade technology while they own the generic Infantry II unit upgrade technology and they have infantry on that unit upgrade card that would be placed in their home system at the start of their next turn, then those infantry are transferred to the <i>Valefar Assimilator</i> card that they are using to copy the faction&ndash;specific infantry unit upgrade.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>
    <li>If the Nekro player copies the <a href="/F_nomad">Nomad</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Flagship:~:text=Memoria"><i>Memoria II</i></a> flagship unit upgrade technology, its attributes and abilities replace those of <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Flagship:~:text=The%20Alastor"><i>The Alastor</i></a>.<sup>1,2</sup></li>
    <li>If the <a href="/F_jol_nar">Jol&ndash;Nar</a> player uses their hero to replace a technology which is currently being copied by a <i>Valefar Assimilator</i>, it will remain copied with a Valefar Assimilator token on it while in that player&rsquo;s technology deck.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <li>For the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition_4:~:text=Adapt%20New%20Strategies"><i>Adapt New Strategies</i></a> objective, a <i>Valefar Assimilator</i> technology will count if and only if it is currently copying another technology.<sup>5</sup></li>
    <li>If the Nekro player has copied certain technology (possibly two or more at different points in time), the following apply:<sup>*</sup></li>
    <ol>
        <li>If both the <a href="/F_saar">Saar</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Clan_of_Saar#Space_Dock:~:text=Floating%20Factory">Floating Factory</a> II unit upgrade and the <a href="/F_vuilraith">Vuil&rsquo;raith</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Vortex"><i>Vortex</i></a> technology are copied, and another player blockades a Nekro space dock, the Nekro player returns any captured units, then destroys the blockaded space dock.<sup>*</sup></li>
        <li>If the Nekro player has copied both the <a href="/F_letnev">Letnev</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Barony_of_Letnev#:~:text=Non-Euclidean%20Shielding"><i>Non&ndash;Euclidean Shielding</i></a> technology and the generic <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Duranium_Armor"><i>Duranium Armor</i></a> technology, then a space combat between the Nekro player and the <a href="/F_letnev">Letnev</a> player in certain circumstances may result in neither player being able to win. If this happens, the attacker must declare a retreat. If the attacker cannot do so, they destroy all their units in that combat.<sup>1</sup></li>
        <li>If both the <a href="/F_muaat">Muaat</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Embers_of_Muaat#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Magmus%20Reactor"><i>Magmus Reactor</i></a> technology and the <a href="/F_saar">Saar</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Clan_of_Saar#Space_Dock:~:text=Floating%20Factory">Floating Factory</a> II unit upgrade are copied, the Nekro player may move their space docks into supernovae.<sup>*</sup></li>
        <li>If the <a href="/F_saar">Saar</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Clan_of_Saar#Space_Dock:~:text=Floating%20Factory">Floating Factory</a> II unit upgrade is copied, both the Nekro player and the <a href="/F_saar">Saar</a> player may have their space docks in the same system, if there are no ships in that system.<sup>*</sup></li>
        <li>If the <a href="/F_norr">N&rsquo;orr</a> player&rsquo;s Exotrireme II unit upgrade is copied, and the Nekro player is in a combat with the <a href="/F_norr">N&rsquo;orr</a> player, then the players will alternate when resolving end of combat round abilities, starting with the active player (all players may resolve abilities in initiative order, but it is most common for only the two players involved in the combat to want to resolve abilities). For example, if the attacking player has two Exotriremes II in the system and the defender has four, assuming both players are hostile toward each other, the most likely sequence is as follows: The attacker activates one of their Exotriremes II, leaving them with one and the defender with two; The defender activates one of their Exotriremes II leaving them with one and the attacker with none.<sup>*</sup></li>
        <li>If the <a href="/F_deepwrought">Deepwrought</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Deepwrought_Scholarate#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Radical%20Advancement"><i>Radical Advancement</i></a> technology is copied, the Nekro player may resolve its ability, and will gain the chosen new technology; they will not gain command tokens.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>
    <li>The Nekro player may lose a technology if they copy a new one. If they lose certain technologies, the following apply:<sup>*</sup></li>
    <ol>
        <li>If the Nekro player loses the <a href="/F_saar">Saar</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Clan_of_Saar#Space_Dock:~:text=Floating%20Factory">Floating Factory</a> II, each space dock the Nekro player controls must be placed on a planet they control in the same system, or the space dock is returned to their reinforcements.<sup>1</sup></li>
        <li>If the Nekro player loses the <a href="/F_muaat">Muaat</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Embers_of_Muaat#War_Sun:~:text=Prototype%20War%20Sun">Prototype War Sun</a> II, and the Nekro player does not have the generic war sun technology, each of their war suns are removed from the game board.<sup>1</sup></li>
        <li>If the <a href="/F_muaat">Muaat</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Embers_of_Muaat#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Magmus%20Reactor"><i>Magmus Reactor</i></a> is lost, the Nekro player&rsquo;s units may remain in any supernovae they are currently in, but cannot move additional units into or through.<sup>2,5</sup></li>
        <li>If the <a href="/F_vuilraith">Vuil&rsquo;raith</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Dimensional%20Tear">Dimensional Tear</a> II is lost, the dimensional tear tokens are removed from under the Nekro player&rsquo;s space docks; the systems are no longer gravity rifts (unless the system tile is a printed gravity rift).<sup>*</sup></li>
        <li>The Nekro player may lose a faction&ndash;specific infantry unit upgrade technology, while they have infantry on the unit upgrade card that would be placed in their home system at the start of their next turn. If they are moving the Valefar Assimilator token to a different faction&ndash;specific infantry unit upgrade technology, the infantry remain on the <i>Valefar Assimilator</i> card. Else, if they own the generic Infantry II unit upgrade technology, the infantry are transferred to that unit upgrade card. Otherwise, the infantry are returned to the Nekro player&rsquo;s reinforcements.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="the-alastor"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Flagship:~:text=The%20Alastor">The Alastor</a> <sub>(Flagship)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Any effect that may target ships or non&ndash;fighter ships may target a ground force that is participating in space combat due to the effect of <i>The Alastor</i>.<sup>1</sup></li>
    <ol>
        <li>This includes counting toward the three non&ndash;fighter ships necessary to trigger the effect of the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Assault_Cannon"><i>Assault Cannon</i></a> technology.<sup>1</sup></li>
        <li>The <a href="/F_winnu">Winnu</a> player&rsquo;s flagship, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Winnu#Flagship:~:text=Salai%20Sai%20Corian"><i>Salai Sai Corian</i></a>, will roll one dice for each infantry the Nekro player has participating in a space combat via the effect of <i>The Alastor</i>.<sup>1,2</sup></li>
    </ol>
    <li>After the Nekro player uses the ability of <i>The Alastor</i>, all other players will have the opportunity to resolve an &ldquo;at the start of combat&rdquo; or an &ldquo;at the start of a round of combat&rdquo; ability before the Nekro player may resolve another ability.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <ol><li>For example, say the Nekro player owns the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Assault_Cannon"><i>Assault Cannon</i></a> technology, and uses the ability of <i>The Alastor</i> to bring the total number of non&ndash;fighter ships in the combat to three (or more). Other players may then resolve one ability each. If their opponent uses an ability that destroys ships, such as from their own <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Assault_Cannon"><i>Assault Cannon</i></a>, to reduce the number of non&ndash;fighter ships the Nekro player has in the combat to two (or fewer), then the Nekro player will be unable to resolve the ability of their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Assault_Cannon"><i>Assault Cannon</i></a>.<sup>*</sup></li></ol>
    <li>Some abilities may destroy <i>The Alastor</i> at the start of a combat before the Nekro player has used its ability, such as the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Assault_Cannon"><i>Assault Cannon</i></a> technology.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>Ground forces on planets remain there while participating in combat.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <ol><li>When the Nekro player is in a space combat against the <a href="/F_argent">Argent</a> player, their infantry on planets participating in the combat cannot be targeted by the ability of the <a href="/F_argent">Argent</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Argent_Flight#Destroyer:~:text=Strike%20Wing%20Alpha%20II"><i>Strike Wing Alpha II</i></a> destroyers.<sup>4</sup></li></ol>
    <li>If <i>The Alastor</i> is destroyed during space combat, any ground forces in that combat remain in that combat.<sup>1</sup></li>
    <li>If the Nekro player copies another player&rsquo;s flagship unit upgrade technology with one of their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Valefar%20Assimilator"><i>Valefar Assimilator</i></a> technologies during a space combat, any ground forces in that combat remain in that combat. If the Nekro player starts the space combat copying another player&rsquo;s flagship unit upgrade technology, ground forces cannot participate in that combat, unless the Nekro player stops copying that flagship unit upgrade technology during the &ldquo;start of combat&rdquo; window.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <ol><li>This applies only to copying another player&rsquo;s flagship unit upgrade technology, currently only the <a href="/F_nomad">Nomad</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Flagship:~:text=Memoria"><i>Memoria II</i></a>, with a <i>Valefar Assimilator</i> X or Y token. Copying a flagship with <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Breakthrough:~:text=Valefar%20Assimilator%20Z"><i>Valefar Assimilator Z</i></a> does not replace the abilities of <i>The Alastor</i>.<sup>1,2</sup></li></ol>
    <li>Ground forces participating in a space combat due to the effect of <i>The Alastor</i> are units that can be transported, so they do not count toward the Nekro player&rsquo;s fleet pool limit.<sup>1,2,5</sup></li>
    <li>If the Nekro player has one of their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Valefar%20Assimilator"><i>Valefar Assimilator</i></a> tokens on the <a href="/F_ul">Ul</a> player&rsquo;s Hel Titan II faction unit upgrade technology, they may use <i>The Alastor</i> to have their PDS in the active system participate in the space combat.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>A ground force participating in a space combat may count toward scoring the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Prophecy_of_Kings_Expansion_3:~:text=Demonstrate%20Your%20Power"><i>Demonstrate Your Power</i></a> secret objective.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If the Nekro player loses their last ground force during a space combat and consequently meets the requirements for elimination, they are immediately eliminated. They will not be given the opportunity to score any objectives from winning the combat or destroying certain units at the same time their last ground force was destroyed.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <ol><li>If the Nekro player uses a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Direct%20Hit"><i>Direct Hit</i></a> action card to destroy an opponent&rsquo;s flagship, they may score the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition_3:~:text=Destroy%20their%20Greatest%20Ship"><i>Destroy Their Greatest Ship</i></a> secret objective, even if there are some hits remaining that will cause the Nekro player to be eliminated once they are assigned. If this would bring the Nekro player to ten victory points, they will instead win the game before they are eliminated.<sup>*</sup></li></ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="nekro-malleon"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Leaders:~:text=Nekro%20Malleon">Nekro Malleon</a> <sub>(Agent)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the chosen player is the <a href="/F_muaat">Muaat</a> player with their commander, Magmus, unlocked, they will gain a trade good from it if they spend a token from their strategy pool when resolving this ability.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <ol><li>That trade good will be gained separately from the other two.<sup>*</sup></li></ol>
    <li>The ability of Nekro Malleon cannot be resolved while another ability is resolving.<sup>4</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="nekro-acidos"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Leaders:~:text=Nekro%20Acidos">Nekro Acidos</a> <sub>(Commander)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>When the Nekro player gains their third technology and unlocks Nekro Acidos, they cannot apply Nekro Acidos to that instance of gaining a technology.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>When the Nekro player places a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Valefar%20Assimilator">Valefar Assimilator</a> token on a technology, they are not gaining a technology.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="polymorphic-algorithm">UNIT.DSGN.FLAYESH &mdash; <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Leaders:~:text=Polymorphic%20Algorithm">Polymorphic Algorithm</a> <sub>(Hero)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>When the other player&rsquo;s units are destroyed, this does not trigger the Nekro player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Technological%20Singularity"><sc>Technological Singularity</sc></a> ability.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>Unit upgrades do not have a color. The Nekro player cannot gain a unit upgrade with <i>Polymorphic Algorithm</i>.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="mordred"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Mech:~:text=Mordred">Mordred</a> <sub>(Mech)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A Mordred will apply +2 against a player with both <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Valefar%20Assimilator">Valefar Assimilator</a> tokens, and not +4.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="valefar-assimilator-z"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Breakthrough:~:text=Valefar%20Assimilator%20Z">Valefar Assimilator Z</a> <sub>(Breakthrough)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the Nekro player places a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Valefar%20Assimilator">Valefar Assimilator</a> X or Y token on the <a href="/F_nomad">Nomad</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Flagship:~:text=Memoria"><i>Memoria II</i></a> unit upgrade technology card, their flagship would still gain each ability granted to them by <i>Valefar Assimilator Z</i> from the flagships of other players.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>The Nekro player cannot place multiple Valefar Assimilator Z tokens on the same player&rsquo;s faction sheet.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>Placing a Valefar Assimilator Z token is not gaining a technology. It does not trigger the ability of Nekro Acidos, the Nekro player&rsquo;s commander.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>If the Nekro player has a Valefar Assimilator Z token on the <a href="/F_mahact">Mahact</a> player&rsquo;s faction sheet, they will always apply the +2 to the combat rolls for <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Flagship:~:text=The%20Alastor"><i>The Alastor</i></a>.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If the Nekro player has a Valefar Assimilator Z token on the <a href="/F_vuilraith">Vuil&rsquo;raith</a> player&rsquo;s faction sheet, copying their flagship, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=The%20Terror%20Between"><i>The Terror Between</i></a>, they will capture destroyed units. They may also capture their own units, and may return their own captured units to their reinforcements at any time.<sup>6</sup></li>
    <li>If the Nekro player copies the <a href="/F_firmament">Firmament</a> player&rsquo;s flagship, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Firmament_/_The_Obsidian#Flagship:~:text=Heaven%27s%20Eye"><i>Heaven&rsquo;s Eye</i></a>, references to &ldquo;your plots&rdquo; refer to the <a href="/F_firmament">Firmament</a> player&rsquo;s plots.<sup>6</sup></li>
    <li>If the Nekro player has copied the <a href="/F_firmament">Firmament</a> player&rsquo;s flagship, and the <a href="/F_firmament">Firmament</a> becomes the <a href="/F_firmament">Obsidian</a>, the Valefar Assimilator Z token is moved to the <a href="/F_firmament">Obsidian</a> player&rsquo;s flagship.<sup>6</sup></li>
    <li>The Nekro player&rsquo;s flagship gains only the text abilities of a copied flagship. Unit abilities, such as <a href="/R_deploy"><sc>Deploy</sc></a>, <a href="/R_space_cannon"><sc>Space Cannon</sc></a> or <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a>, are not copied.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>If a player is eliminated while the Nekro player has a Valefar Assimilator Z token on their faction sheet, the Nekro player keeps the copied flagship abilities; that faction sheet remains in play for this purpose.<sup>6</sup></li>
    </ol>
</article>
